# L §2.3 (tally 2.1.2, issue #29): a `ties by` term counts one level, as a `from` term does. An aggregate's `ties by`
# takes one term (parse rule 7), which may be another aggregate with its own `ties by`: here 8 links, and inside the
# 8th link's parentheses the depth is 8 terms + 1 bracket = 9.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

index ks = [k1, k2]

def w[k in ks]: int = 1

def z: key ks = argmin(w[k] for k in ks) ties by argmin(w[k] for k in ks) ties by argmin(w[k] for k in ks) ties by argmin(w[k] for k in ks) ties by argmin(w[k] for k in ks) ties by argmin(w[k] for k in ks) ties by argmin(w[k] for k in ks) ties by argmin(w[k] for k in ks) ties by argmin(w[k] for k in ks)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DEPTH ...
